    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1782">

                <pb facs="1163" n="1047" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg1047"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.74/58.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Price to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 253.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 14, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Supplementing my telegram of July 25,
                    1914, * * * I have the honor to report that Sr. Lefevre a few days ago stated
                    that Panama would agree to whatever we might demand in this matter * * * and
                    promised to give me a formal note to this effect. This note came this afternoon
                    and a copy of it and its translation are herewith enclosed. The note, however,
                    is quite different from what I was led to expect. * * *</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. Jennings Price</hi></signed>.</closer>


                <xi:include href="d1782-a1.xml" xpointer="d1782-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
